  "question": {
    "text": "Let the maximum area of the triangle that can be inscribed in the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, having one of its vertices at one end of the major axis of the ellipse and one of its sides parallel to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis, be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>. Then the eccentricity of the ellipse is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
